# ShellCheck configuration for scripts/ci/ — applies to every script in this
# directory (ShellCheck reads the .shellcheckrc nearest the file being checked).
#
# Four gates source scripts/ci/pr-body-input.sh unconditionally:
# deliverables-check.sh, validate-pr-body.sh, ffmpeg-patches-surface-check.sh
# and state-md-touch-check.sh. The pre-commit hook passes only the staged
# files, so when one of those four is staged without the helper, ShellCheck
# cannot see the sibling and emits SC1091 "not specified as input" — a red
# hook for a file that is fine.
#
# external-sources makes ShellCheck follow the `# shellcheck source=` directives
# those four already carry. It is not a suppression: it turns the sibling into
# analysed code instead of an unread file, so the checker sees MORE, not less.
# Measured over all 57 scripts/ci/*.sh checked one at a time (the shape the
# pre-commit hook uses): 4 findings before, 0 after, nothing new introduced.
external-sources=true
